  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Since GitHub is already whitelisted for image/string loading under `*.github.io` for GitHub Pages, having `raw.githubusercontent.com` whitelisted alongside it would be very convenient. \n\nJust as a small example, by using the `raw.githubusercontent.com` domain, this would allow a world creator to load images or text/JSON data from a public repository from a specific historical commit or branch of that Git repository by its URL, which is handy for loading data for a specific version of the repository, without having to make a new folder for each version and have duplicate data in those folders.\n\nI understand it might be a bit of an edge-case, but since it's pretty much the same content as served from `*.github.io`, it might as well be added to the whitelist alongside it.",
